Z/4[x]/(x^2 + 1)
  16 elements (4^2), characteristic 4
  a field: no; an integral domain: no (4 is not prime, so Z/4 already has zero divisors)
  units: 8; zero divisors: 7 nonzero (by brute force over all products)
> irreducible x^8 + x^4 + x^3 + x + 1 over GF(2)
x^8 + x^4 + x^3 + x + 1 is irreducible over GF(2)
  how: Rabin's test (degree 8: x^(q^8) = x mod f, and gcd(x^(q^(8/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 8; q = 2)
  check: Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp: 1 distinct irreducible factor; trial division by every monic polynomial of degree <= 4: none divides
> primitive x^8 + x^4 + x^3 + x + 1 over GF(2)
x^8 + x^4 + x^3 + x + 1 is irreducible over GF(2)
  how: Rabin's test (degree 8: x^(q^8) = x mod f, and gcd(x^(q^(8/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 8; q = 2)
  check: Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp: 1 distinct irreducible factor; trial division by every monic polynomial of degree <= 4: none divides
not primitive: x has order 51 < q^8 - 1 = 255
  how: x^((q^n - 1)/r) != 1 mod f for each prime r | q^n - 1 = 3 * 5 * 17
  so an LFSR with this feedback polynomial has period 51
  check: stepping x, x^2, ... mod f: x^k = 1 first at k = 51
> primitive x^8 + x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + 1 over GF(2)
x^8 + x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + 1 is irreducible over GF(2)
  how: Rabin's test (degree 8: x^(q^8) = x mod f, and gcd(x^(q^(8/r)) - x, f) = 1 for each prime r | 8; q = 2)
  check: Ben-Or's test agrees; Berlekamp: 1 distinct irreducible factor; trial division by every monic polynomial of degree <= 4: none divides
primitive: x has order 255 = q^8 - 1 = 255
  how: x^((q^n - 1)/r) != 1 mod f for each prime r | q^n - 1 = 3 * 5 * 17
  so an LFSR with this feedback polynomial has period 255 (maximal: every nonzero state)
  check: stepping x, x^2, ... mod f: x^k = 1 first at k = 255
> factor x^4 + 1 over GF(2)
x^4 + 1 = (x + 1)^4 over GF(2)
  how: square-free split (gcd(f, f'), p-th roots where f' = 0), distinct-degree split (gcd(x^(q^i) - x, f)), Cantor-Zassenhaus equal-degree split (by the trace map)
  check: the product of the factors is f; each factor is irreducible (Rabin)
  roots in GF(2): 1 by evaluation at every element, the number of distinct linear factors (1)
> factor x^8 - 1 mod 3
x^8 + 2 = (x + 1) (x + 2) (x^2 + 1) (x^2 + x + 2) (x^2 + 2x + 2) over GF(3)
  how: square-free split (gcd(f, f'), p-th roots where f' = 0), distinct-degree split (gcd(x^(q^i) - x, f)), Cantor-Zassenhaus equal-degree split
  check: the product of the factors is f; each factor is irreducible (Rabin); Berlekamp counts 5 distinct factors
  roots in GF(3): 2 by evaluation at every element, the number of distinct linear factors (2)
> factor x^15 - 1 over GF(2)
x^15 + 1 = (x + 1) (x^2 + x + 1) (x^4 + x + 1) (x^4 + x^3 + 1) (x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + x + 1) over GF(2)
  how: square-free split (gcd(f, f'), p-th roots where f' = 0), distinct-degree split (gcd(x^(q^i) - x, f)), Cantor-Zassenhaus equal-degree split (by the trace map)
  check: the product of the factors is f; each factor is irreducible (Rabin); Berlekamp counts 5 distinct factors
  roots in GF(2): 1 by evaluation at every element, the number of distinct linear factors (1)
> factor x^6 + 1 over GF(4)
x^6 + 1 = (x + 1)^2 (x + 0x2)^2 (x + 0x3)^2 over GF(2^2)
  how: square-free split (gcd(f, f'), p-th roots where f' = 0), distinct-degree split (gcd(x^(q^i) - x, f)), Cantor-Zassenhaus equal-degree split (by the trace map)
  check: the product of the factors is f; each factor is irreducible (Rabin)
  roots in GF(2^2): 3 by evaluation at every element, the number of distinct linear factors (3)
> factor crc16 over GF(2)
  note: crc16 is the CRC-16 (IBM/ANSI) polynomial x^16 + x^15 + x^2 + 1
x^16 + x^15 + x^2 + 1 = (x + 1) (x^15 + x + 1) over GF(2)
  how: square-free split (gcd(f, f'), p-th roots where f' = 0), distinct-degree split (gcd(x^(q^i) - x, f)), Cantor-Zassenhaus equal-degree split (by the trace map)
  check: the product of the factors is f; each factor is irreducible (Rabin); Berlekamp counts 2 distinct factors
  roots in GF(2): 1 by evaluation at every element, the number of distinct linear factors (1)
> order crc32 over GF(2)
  note: crc32 is the CRC-32 (IEEE 802.3) polynomial x^32 + x^26 + x^23 + x^22 + x^16 + x^12 + x^11 + x^10 + x^8 + x^7 + x^5 + x^4 + x^2 + x + 1
the order of x mod x^32 + x^26 + x^23 + x^22 + x^16 + x^12 + x^11 + x^10 + x^8 + x^7 + x^5 + x^4 + x^2 + x + 1 over GF(2): 4294967295
  the period of an LFSR (or of a CRC's register) with this feedback polynomial: x^4294967295 = 1 mod f
  how: factor f; for an irreducible factor of degree d the order divides q^d - 1; a factor to the power e multiplies it by the least p^t >= e; the lcm over the factors
  check: x^4294967295 = 1 mod f and x^(4294967295/r) != 1 for each prime r | 4294967295 = 3 * 5 * 17 * 257 * 65537 (repeated squaring): so the order is exactly that
> roots x^2 + 1 mod 5
roots of x^2 + 1 in GF(5): 2 3
  how: the linear factors (gcd with x^q - x, then Cantor-Zassenhaus)
  check: evaluation at all 5 elements: 2 roots
> roots x^2 - 1 mod 8
roots of x^2 + 7 in Z/8: 4: 1 3 5 7
  how: evaluation at every element (Z/8 is not a field: a polynomial can have more roots than its degree)
> poly (x + 1)^5 mod 5
(x + 1)^5 = x^5 + 1 over GF(5)
  how: polynomial arithmetic with coefficients in GF(5)
> gcd x^4 - 1, x^6 - 1 mod 7
gcd(x^4 + 6, x^6 + 6) = x^2 + 6 over GF(7)
  how: Euclid; Bezout: (6x^2)(x^4 + 6) + (1)(x^6 + 6) = x^2 + 6
  check: the Bezout sum is the gcd; the gcd divides both
