  ucas: order x^4 + x + 1 over gf(2)
the order of x mod x^4 + x + 1 over GF(2): 15
  the period of an LFSR (or of a CRC's register) with this feedback polynomial: x^15 = 1 mod f
  how: factor f; for an irreducible factor of degree d the order divides q^d - 1; a factor to the power e multiplies it by the least p^t >= e; the lcm over the factors
  check: stepping x, x^2, ... mod f: x^k = 1 first at k = 15
> what is the minimal polynomial of 0x02 in GF(2^8)
  ucas: ring gf(2^8) minpoly 0x02
  note: integers are elements in integer notation (the coefficients as base-2 digits): 0x02 = x
0x02 = x in GF(2^8)
  inverse: 0x8e = x^7 + x^3 + x^2 + x (a^(q-2))
  check: 0x02 * 0x8e = 0x01 (by log tables)
  order 255 (divides 255): a generator
  log base 0x02: 1 (0x02^1 = 0x02)
  minimal polynomial over GF(2): x^8 + x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + 1 (degree 8: a lies in GF(2^8))
  conjugates a^(2^i): 0x02 0x04 0x10 0x1d 0x4c 0x9d 0x5f 0x85
  check: the minimal polynomial is irreducible (Rabin) and vanishes at a: 0x00
